@page "/p/privacy"
@using FileUploader.Models
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject IOptions<InstanceOptions> Instance

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy</PageTitle>

<div class="info-page">
    <div class="info-section">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h1 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="section-meta">Last updated: September 18, 2026 - View code on <a href="https://github.com/maikatura/PubUpload" target="_blank ">github</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="section-text">@Instance.Value.Name operates a file hosting service that allows users to upload and share files. This Privacy Notice explains how we collect, use, and disclose information when you use our service.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="section-text">Each file upload generates its own independent record containing only:</p>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li><strong>File Metadata</strong> &mdash; File type, size, upload timestamp, and unique URL. Original file names are never stored on the server.</li>
            <li><strong>Image Metadata Removal</strong> &mdash; EXIF, GPS location, XMP and comments are stripped from JPEG, PNG, WebP and GIF images before they are saved.</li>
            <li><strong>Public Content</strong> &mdash; The uploaded file itself, publicly accessible via its unique URL.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout callout-info">
            <strong>Note:</strong> No IP addresses or User-Agent strings are collected or stored. The &ldquo;Your Files&rdquo; list is kept in your browser&rsquo;s local storage on your device only and never transmitted to us.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">3. Upload Limits</h2>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li><strong>Maximum File Size:</strong> 100 MB per upload.</li>
            <li><strong>Storage Duration:</strong> All files are stored for a maximum of @Instance.Value.RetentionDays days, then automatically deleted.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li><strong>Limiting Liability</strong> &mdash; We take no responsibility for user-generated content; you are accountable for what you upload.</li>
            <li><strong>Service Operation</strong> &mdash; To generate unique URLs and manage file storage.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">5. Public Nature of Files</h2>
        <div class="callout callout-warning">
            <strong>Important:</strong> Our service is designed for public sharing.
        </div>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li>Any file uploaded is publicly accessible to anyone with the direct URL. No login is required to view or download files.</li>
            <li>By uploading a file, you acknowledge that the content will be publicly accessible on the internet.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">6. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li><strong>No Logs:</strong> Server logs do not contain file names, URLs, or IP addresses.</li>
            <li><strong>Automatic Deletion:</strong> After @Instance.Value.RetentionDays days, the file and all associated metadata are permanently deleted.</li>
            <li><strong>Local Upload History:</strong> The list of your uploads is stored in your browser&rsquo;s local storage. Deleting your browser data removes it; we have no copy of it.</li>
            <li><strong>Manual Deletion:</strong> Users may delete their files at any time. Only that specific file's data is removed.</li>
            <li><strong>Independent Records:</strong> Deleting one file does not affect data from other uploads.</li>
            <li><strong>Third-Party Copies:</strong> Once a URL is shared, we cannot control or delete copies cached by others.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <div class="callout callout-danger">
            <strong>@Instance.Value.Name operates under a strict "No Responsibility" policy regarding user-generated content.</strong>
        </div>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li>You are solely responsible for the content you upload.</li>
            <li>We are not liable for any damages, losses, or consequences arising from your uploads.</li>
            <li>You agree to indemnify @Instance.Value.Name from any claims resulting from your use of the service.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">8. Security Measures</h2>
        <ul class="section-list">
            <li><strong>Security Headers:</strong> X-Frame-Options (DENY), X-Content-Type-Options (nosniff), Referrer-Policy (no-referrer), and a restrictive Permissions-Policy are applied to all responses.</li>
            <li><strong>CORS:</strong> API upload endpoints are restricted to our own domains only.</li>
            <li><strong>No Tracking:</strong> We do not use cookies, analytics, advertisements, or third-party tracking scripts.</li>
            <li><strong>No External Fonts:</strong> All fonts are served locally; no connections to third-party CDNs.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-section">
        <h2 class="section-subtitle">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="section-text">We may update this Privacy Notice from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last Updated" date.</p>
    </div>
</div>
